--   **Exact Spacetime Atlas IX residual interface**
--
--   This definition bundle records the two residual equations used in the compactified source bridge. `GenericMRelation` relates the generic $M$ residual to the actual $M$ residual and the source defect. `UnabsorbedResidualIdentity` records the original weighted compatibility equation before the $x\,\lambda_M$ absorption term is moved to the left-hand side.
--
--   The interface follows the radial residual organization of the five-dimensional equal-spin Einstein–Maxwell system. The physical ODE reduction and equal-magnitude angular-momentum setting are documented in [Kunz, Navarro-Lérida and Petersen, *Five-Dimensional Charged Rotating Black Holes*](https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0503010) and [Kunz, Navarro-Lérida and Viebahn, *Charged Rotating Black Holes in Odd Dimensions*](https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605075). The constrained autonomous boundary-value formulation with singular endpoints is discussed in [Fröb, Khavkine, Málek and Pravda, *On well-posedness and algebraic type of the five-dimensional charged rotating black hole with two equal-magnitude angular momenta*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.13266).
--
--   The predicates are explicit theorem inputs. They do not assert existence of a black-hole solution or a metric-valued Ricci correspondence.
